WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.557
EmbedIDE is a native Rust IDE for embedded and systems development.

00:00:03.607 --> 00:00:04.988
It lives in your terminal.

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:10.748
It combines a Vim-style editor, an explorer, an integrated terminal,

00:00:10.798 --> 00:00:16.360
builds with jump-to-source diagnostics, a view for the binaries you produce, and optional AI agents.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:19.322
One Rust binary, with no Electron and no browser.

00:00:20.222 --> 00:00:23.100
Under the hood it is a Cargo workspace of nine crates.

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:27.681
The editor engine has no I/O and no terminal types, so a native GUI could reuse it later.

00:00:27.731 --> 00:00:31.602
The build engine makes a reviewable plan and then runs it, without a shell.

00:00:31.652 --> 00:00:35.285
There is no unsafe code, processes are launched with argument vectors,

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:37.222
and files are written atomically.

00:00:37.272 --> 00:00:41.236
The GUI itself is planned, not started: this alpha is a terminal application.

00:00:42.236 --> 00:00:43.915
This is the real program.

00:00:43.965 --> 00:00:49.362
Open a file from the explorer, press F5, and GCC's error appears in the problems list with file,

00:00:49.412 --> 00:00:50.619
line and column.

00:00:50.669 --> 00:00:51.981
Enter jumps to it.

00:00:53.218 --> 00:00:58.706
Fix, build again, and use the integrated terminal: a real shell in a pseudo-terminal, one key away.

00:01:03.989 --> 00:01:05.796
Open the program you just built.

00:01:05.846 --> 00:01:09.323
A hex viewer and editor, an ELF inspector with sections and symbols,

00:01:09.373 --> 00:01:11.597
and a disassembly view that runs objdump.

00:01:11.647 --> 00:01:15.542
The file is only read, unless you explicitly edit bytes and confirm the save.

00:01:16.542 --> 00:01:21.801
AI integration uses the Claude Code and Codex command-line tools you already have installed and

00:01:21.851 --> 00:01:22.729
logged in.

00:01:22.779 --> 00:01:26.079
EmbedIDE needs no API key, never reads their credentials,

00:01:26.129 --> 00:01:29.223
and removes API key variables from their environment,

00:01:29.273 --> 00:01:33.191
so a subscription request can never silently become billed API usage.

00:01:34.191 --> 00:01:36.583
In agent mode, a plain message is a task.

00:01:36.633 --> 00:01:39.572
Here Claude Code adds a function, edits three files,

00:01:39.622 --> 00:01:42.761
builds with the project's compiler and runs the program.

00:01:42.811 --> 00:01:47.943
EmbedIDE answers each permission request from a policy: edits and builds inside the project run,

00:01:47.993 --> 00:01:53.125
while deleting files, network access, hardware tools and anything outside the project ask first.

00:01:54.025 --> 00:01:58.759
You choose the compilers: GCC, Clang, zig cc, a cross GCC for Cortex-M, NASM.

00:01:58.809 --> 00:02:03.994
EmbedIDE detects what is installed and never installs or flashes anything on its own.

00:02:04.044 --> 00:02:09.003
Debugging with GDB and OpenOCD, and a serial monitor, exist as explicit commands,

00:02:09.053 --> 00:02:12.098
but they are not yet verified on real hardware.

00:02:12.998 --> 00:02:14.226
This is an alpha.

00:02:14.276 --> 00:02:16.219
Linux is the verified platform.

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:18.773
FreeBSD compiles but has not been run yet.

00:02:18.823 --> 00:02:23.270
Windows and macOS are not supported, and the native GUI is planned, not started.

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:28.976
To try it, one command downloads a static build into your home directory and verifies its checksum.

00:02:29.026 --> 00:02:31.998
Then embed doctor shows what EmbedIDE found on your machine.

00:02:41.747 --> 00:02:45.088
To build from source you need Rust one point eighty-five or newer.

00:02:45.138 --> 00:02:48.984
Clone the repository, run cargo build with the release flag, and start embed.

00:02:50.747 --> 00:02:52.675
EmbedIDE is open source under the GPL.

00:02:52.725 --> 00:02:54.395
Try it, and tell us what breaks.

00:02:54.445 --> 00:02:56.072
The link is in the description.
